    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67-a1">

                <pb facs="0142" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg94"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 221.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 10,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am instructed by the Secretary of State
                    to inform you that a gold watch has been sent by the President to the United
                    States consul-general at Shanghai, to be delivered to Captain Stewart, of the
                    Chinese gunboat Sin Ching, as a testimonial of his appreciation of services
                    rendered by Captain Stewart to the American ship Enoch Train when in distress
                    near Hong-Kong. He has also directed me to ask Your Imperial Highness to convey
                    to the same gentleman, through the appropriate channel, the thanks of the United
                    States for the important services rendered by him on the occasion adverted
                    to.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To His Imperial Highness <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince Kung</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
